      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142932",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a sample of size $n = 120$ from a normal population. Given that the sample standard deviation is $s = 3$, find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population standard deviation $\u03c3$ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(X > 162.481) = 0.005$ and $P(X < 83.018) = 0.005$, where $X\u223c\u03c7^{2}(119)$ has a chi-square distribution with $119$ degrees of freedom.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
