      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143366",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a sample of size $n = 82$ from a normal population. Given that the sample standard deviation is $s = 2.5$, find a $90%$ confidence interval for the population standard deviation $\u03c3$ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(X > 103.010) = 0.05$ and $P(X < 61.261) = 0.05$, where $X\u223c\u03c7^{2}(81)$ has a chi-square distribution with $81$ degrees of freedom.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
